#: ../../../how-to/enable-smart-cards-in-snapped-browsers.md:0
msgid ""
"Configure Firefox or Chromium installed from a snap to use your smart card "
"for authentication and signing content."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/enable-smart-cards-in-snapped-browsers.md:7
msgid "Topics: Security"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/enable-smart-cards-in-snapped-browsers.md:11
msgid "Enable smart cards in snapped browsers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/enable-smart-cards-in-snapped-browsers.md:13
msgid ""
"<!--\n"
"Authors: Marek Suchánek <marek.suchanek@canonical.com>, Nathan Teodosio "
"<nathan.teodosio@canonical.com>\n"
"-->\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/enable-smart-cards-in-snapped-browsers.md:17
msgid ""
"Enable smart card authentication in Firefox or Chromium installed from snap."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/enable-smart-cards-in-snapped-browsers.md:19
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/enable-smart-cards-in-snapped-browsers.md:21
msgid ""
"With this configuration, you can use your smart card to authenticate and "
"sign content in Firefox or Chromium installed from snap. By default, smart "
"cards do not work in snapped web browsers due to strict confinement in the "
"snap."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/enable-smart-cards-in-snapped-browsers.md:23
msgid ""
"If instead you want to use your smart card to **log in and authenticate the "
"user**, see {ref}`log-in-using-a-smart-card`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/enable-smart-cards-in-snapped-browsers.md:25
msgid "What you’ll need"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/enable-smart-cards-in-snapped-browsers.md:27
msgid ""
"A web browser installed from snap: [Firefox](https://snapcraft.io/firefox) "
"or [Chromium](https://snapcraft.io/chromium)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/enable-smart-cards-in-snapped-browsers.md:29
msgid ""
"A smart card, ideally one that is [supported by OpenSC](https://github.com/"
"OpenSC/OpenSC/wiki/Supported-hardware-%28smart-cards-and-USB-tokens%29)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/enable-smart-cards-in-snapped-browsers.md:31
msgid "Select your smart card driver"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/enable-smart-cards-in-snapped-browsers.md:33
msgid ""
"Check if your smart card is supported by OpenSC. See [Supported hardware "
"(smart cards and USB tokens)](https://github.com/OpenSC/OpenSC/wiki/"
"Supported-hardware-%28smart-cards-and-USB-tokens%29)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/enable-smart-cards-in-snapped-browsers.md:35
msgid ""
"If you can see your smart card on the list, you can skip this whole section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/enable-smart-cards-in-snapped-browsers.md:37
msgid ""
"If your smart card isn't supported by OpenSC, you need a binary driver for "
"your smart card. Your organization or government usually provides this "
"driver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/enable-smart-cards-in-snapped-browsers.md:40
msgid ""
"Using third-party smart card drivers in snap is experimental and "
"unsupported. The driver might not work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/enable-smart-cards-in-snapped-browsers.md:43
msgid ""
"Install the smart card driver that you received from your organization or "
"government. For example, **Bit4id** cards require the `libbit4xpki.so` "
"driver, which is a proprietary `p11k` library. When you install the driver, "
"it's available at the `/usr/lib/libbit4xpki.so` file path."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/enable-smart-cards-in-snapped-browsers.md:45
msgid ""
"In the following commands, **replace** `libbit4xpki.so` with the file name "
"of your driver and `/usr/lib/libbit4xpki.so` with the full path to the "
"driver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/enable-smart-cards-in-snapped-browsers.md:47
msgid ""
"Move the smart card driver, such as `libbit4xpki.so`, into the snap "
"environment in your home directory."
msgstr ""

