msgid ""
"Replace `MY_USER_NAME` with your user name, `Bit4id` with your smart card "
"name or brand and `libbit4xpki.so` with the proprietary driver file name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/enable-smart-cards-in-snapped-browsers.md:177
msgid "Test if the authentication works"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/enable-smart-cards-in-snapped-browsers.md:179
msgid "Open your web browser and try authenticating with your smart card."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/enable-smart-cards-in-snapped-browsers.md:181
msgid "Did it work? If not:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/enable-smart-cards-in-snapped-browsers.md:183
msgid "Report any bugs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/enable-smart-cards-in-snapped-browsers.md:185
msgid ""
"If your card is supported by OpenSC and you encounter an issue with the "
"workflow, please add your comment to [OpenSC smart cards do not work in the "
"snapped browsers (LP#2089141)](https://launchpad.net/bugs/2089141)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/enable-smart-cards-in-snapped-browsers.md:187
msgid ""
"If you provided a proprietary smart card driver, it might not work for a "
"variety of reasons. Please file a new issue at [Launchpad Bugs](https://"
"launchpad.net/bugs)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/enable-smart-cards-in-snapped-browsers.md:189
msgid ""
"Your driver might depend on missing libraries. See the full list of "
"dependencies and attach them to your bug report:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/enable-smart-cards-in-snapped-browsers.md:199
msgid ""
"Replace `libbit4xpki.so` with your driver's file name. Replace `firefox` "
"with `chromium` if you use Chromium."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/enable-smart-cards-in-snapped-browsers.md:201
msgid ""
"If your card isn't supported by OpenSC, see the known issue tracked in "
